{
  "summary": "The PR introduces a `ShieldsPresets` utility to manage managed filter lists (Standard, Balanced, Strict) while preserving custom/regional subscriptions. It correctly implements idempotence, category-specific toggles, and identity checks using URL strings to avoid DNS hazards. The logic ensures that non-managed URLs are never overwritten or removed during preset transitions. Tests cover transition integrity, category isolation, and identity strictness.",
  "approved": true,
  "bugs": [],
  "architecture_issues": [
    "The `replace` method uses `selected.addAll(target)` which may introduce duplicates if a target URL was already present in the `selected` set (though `LinkedHashSet` handles uniqueness, the order might shift slightly)."
  ],
  "security_issues": [],
  "test_gaps": [
    "No test case specifically verifies the behavior when a managed URL is provided with a different protocol (e.g., http vs https) to ensure it doesn't accidentally match/overwrite."
  ],
  "recommended_changes": [
    "Consider using `Set.addAll` explicitly or checking for existence before adding to `selected` to maintain strict order consistency.",
    ""
  ]
}
